> (not the 10 specified in the analysis brief). <strong>New York, Tokyo, and Los Angeles</strong> are absent from the dataset. Additionally, <strong>Paris and Sydney have zero valid price entries</strong> (100% null in the <code>price</code> column), meaning all pricing statistics for these two cities are unavailable. Bangkok prices appear inflated (median $1,400/night), suggesting the values may not be normalized to USD — interpret Bangkok pricing with caution. All figures below are derived exclusively from non-null data; no imputation or fabrication was applied.", "+  <strong>Data Integrity Note</strong> &mdash; This dataset contains 50,000 listings across <strong>7 cities</strong>. <strong>New York, Tokyo, and Los Angeles</strong> &mdash; three of the ten cities specified in the analysis brief &mdash; are absent from the dataset. <strong>Paris and Sydney have zero valid price entries</strong> (100% null in the <code>price</code> column); all pricing statistics for these two cities are unavailable. Bangkok prices (median $1,400/night) appear to be in local currency (THB) rather than USD &mdash; interpret Bangkok pricing with caution. All figures derive exclusively from non-null data; no imputation or fabrication was applied.", " </div>", " ", " <!-- KPI Dashboard -->", " <section>", "   <h2>Executive KPI Dashboard</h2>", "   <div class="kpi-grid">", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="label">Total Listings</div>", "-      <div class="value">50,000</div>", "-      <div class="context">Across 7 cities</div>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="label">Highest Median Price</div>", "-      <div class="value">$1,400</div>", "-      <div class="context">Bangkok (currency caveat)</div>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="label">Lowest Median Price</div>", "-      <div class="value">$131</div>", "-      <div class="context">Rome</div>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="label">Highest Pro Host Share</div>", "-      <div class="value">60.4%</div>", "-      <div class="context">Bangkok</div>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="label">Highest Guest Demand</div>", "-      <div class="value">1.77 revs/mo</div>", "-      <div class="context">Rome</div>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="label">Highest Entire Home Share</div>", "-      <div class="value">88.2%</div>", "-      <div class="context">Paris</div>", "-    </div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="label">Total Listings</div><div class="value">50,000</div><div class="context">Across 7 cities (3 missing)</div></div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="label">Highest Median Price</div><div class="value">$1,400</div><div class="context">Bangkok (likely THB, not USD)</div></div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="label">Lowest Median Price</div><div class="value">$131</div><div class="context">Rome (validated USD)</div></div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="label">Highest Pro Host Share</div><div class="value">60.4%</div><div class="context">Bangkok</div></div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="label">Highest Guest Demand</div><div class="value">1.77 rev/mo</div><div class="context">Rome</div></div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="label">Highest Entire Home Share</div><div class="value">88.2%</div><div class="context">Paris</div></div>", "   </div>", " </section>", " ", " <!-- Section 1: Market Overview -->", " <section id="market-overview">", "   <h2>1. Global Market Overview</h2>", "-  <p>This section establishes the scale and composition of each city's Airbnb market — total listings, room-type breakdown, and overall market structure. London dominates by volume, followed distantly by Paris; together they account for <strong>61.2%</strong> of all listings in the dataset.</p>", "+  <p>London and Paris dominate by volume, together accounting for <strong>61.2%</strong> of all listings. Amsterdam is the smallest market (3.5%) but has the most constrained supply dynamics. Entire homes dominate across all cities; shared and hotel rooms are negligible.</p>", " ", "   <div class="chart-row">", "-    <div class="chart-box">", "-      <h4>Total Listings by City</h4>", "-      <canvas id="chart-listings"></canvas>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="chart-box">", "-      <h4>Room Type Distribution by City (%)</h4>", "-      <canvas id="chart-roomtype"></canvas>", "-    </div>", "+    <div class="chart-box"><h4>Total Listings by City</h4><canvas id="chart-listings"></canvas></div>", "+    <div class="chart-box"><h4>Room Type Distribution by City (%)</h4><canvas id="chart-roomtype"></canvas></div>", "   </div>", " ", "   <h3>Market Composition Table</h3>", "   <div class="card">", "     <table class="data-table">", "-      <thead>", "-        <tr>", "-          <th>City</th>", "-          <th class="num">Total Listings</th>", "-          <th class="num">% of Dataset</th>", "-          <th class="num">Entire Home %</th>", "-          <th class="num">Private Room %</th>", "-          <th class="num">Hotel Room %</th>", "-          <th class="num">Shared Room %</th>", "-        </tr>", "-      </thead>", "+      <thead><tr><th>City</th><th class="num">Total Listings</th><th class="num">% of Dataset</th><th class="num">Entire Home %</th><th class="num">Private Room %</th><th class="num">Hotel Room %</th><th class="num">Shared Room %</th></tr></thead>", "       <tbody>", "         <tr><td>London</td><td class="num">16,674</td><td class="num">33.3%</td><td class="num">64.7%</td><td class="num">34.9%</td><td class="num">0.1%</td><td class="num">0.2%</td></tr>", "         <tr><td>Paris</td><td class="num">13,927</td><td class="num">27.9%</td><td class="num">88.2%</td><td class="num">10.7%</td><td class="num">0.9%</td><td class="num">0.2%</td></tr>"]}, {"oldStart": 376, "oldLines": 238, "newStart": 196, "newLines": 156, "lines": ["   </div>", " ", "   <div class="callout">", "-    <strong>Key Insight:</strong> Paris and Amsterdam are the most "commercialized" markets by room type, with over 82% of listings categorized as entire homes. Barcelona stands out as having the highest share of private rooms (38.9%), suggesting a more diverse, possibly more resident-driven supply mix. Hotel and shared rooms are negligible across all cities (&lt;2% combined).", "+    <strong>Key Insight:</strong> Paris and Amsterdam are the most "entire-home-heavy" markets (88% and 83%), while Barcelona has the most balanced room-type mix (60% entire home, 39% private room). This reflects different supply models: owner-occupied private-room hosting vs. dedicated entire-property rentals.", "   </div>", " </section>", " ", " <!-- Section 2: Pricing Analysis -->", " <section id="pricing-analysis">", "   <h2>2. Pricing Dynamics Across Cities</h2>", "-  <p>Price analysis is limited to <strong>5 of 7 cities</strong> with valid price data. Paris and Sydney (43.9% of all listings) have entirely null <code>price</code> columns and are excluded from pricing charts. Bangkok's values appear to be in local currency (THB) rather than USD; treat Bangkok figures as directionally indicative only.</p>", "+  <p>Price analysis covers <strong>5 of 7 cities</strong>. Paris and Sydney (43.9% of listings combined) have entirely null prices. Bangkok values appear to be in local currency (THB) &mdash; at ~34 THB/USD, the true median would be approximately $41, making it the cheapest market.</p>", " ", "   <div class="chart-row">", "-    <div class="chart-box">", "-      <h4>Median &amp; Mean Nightly Price by City (USD)</h4>", "-      <canvas id="chart-price-median"></canvas>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="chart-box">", "-      <h4>Price Distribution by City (Box Plot — IQR, Median)</h4>", "-      <canvas id="chart-price-box"></canvas>", "-    </div>", "+    <div class="chart-box"><h4>Median &amp; Mean Nightly Price by City (USD)</h4><canvas id="chart-price-m