hosts command a premium in Barcelona (+51%), London (+37%), and Rome (+24%). In Amsterdam, the relationship is inverted: professional hosts charge slightly less ($215 vs. $225) than individuals &mdash; likely reflecting regulatory constraints that prevent commercial operators from offering high-end properties. Bangkok shows no meaningful premium (+2.8%), consistent with its deeply commercialized market where pricing is competitive across host types.", "+  </div>", " </section>", " ", " <!-- Section 3: Supply Structure & Host Concentration -->", " <section id="supply-structure">", "   <h2>3. Supply Structure &amp; Host Concentration</h2>", "-  <p>Host concentration — measured as the share of listings controlled by hosts with 5 or more properties — is a strategically critical metric. High professional-host concentration signals a commercially driven market, with implications for regulation, investment risk, and competitive dynamics.</p>", "+  <p>Host concentration &mdash; measured as the share of <em>listings</em> controlled by hosts with 5 or more properties &mdash; is a strategically critical metric informing regulatory risk, market maturity, and competitive dynamics.</p>", " ", "   <div class="chart-row">", "-    <div class="chart-box">", "-      <h4>Professional Host Share by City (% of listings with 5+ properties)</h4>", "-      <canvas id="chart-prof-share"></canvas>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="chart-box">", "-      <h4>Host Portfolio Size Distribution</h4>", "-      <canvas id="chart-host-tiers"></canvas>", "-    </div>", "+    <div class="chart-box"><h4>Professional Host Share by City (% of listings from hosts with 5+ properties)</h4><canvas id="chart-prof-share"></canvas></div>", "+    <div class="chart-box"><h4>Host Portfolio Size Distribution (% of listings by host tier)</h4><canvas id="chart-host-tiers"></canvas></div>", "   </div>", " ", "   <h3>Host Concentration Table</h3>", "   <div class="card">", "     <table class="data-table">", "-      <the